ed, so it is not treated as an unrelated mutation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ba5f1d95adbf4672","cmd-543d2c2da03e4926","cmd-7306666a7b114499","cmd-3b1774e78e3c413c","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state, interruption-recovery, and restart evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, a distinct post-restart identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, content, connectivity, and platform state. Minor hygiene deductions reflect one ineffective troubleshooting restart and three retained temporary evidence files.","limitations":["Isolation was tested from each managed peer and corroborated by loopback-only socket bindings; no separate unmanaged third host was available in the captured topology.","The initial tunnel service configuration caused a transient restart loop before correction, but final and post-restart observations show no failed service or retained broken configuration."]}
